Command Purpose <code>create</code> create a group, rect, image or shader node under a parent <code>attach</code> put a surface without an owner under a parent; the caller becomes its owner <code>update</code> change node properties <code>animate</code> change properties over a duration with an easing curve <code>move</code> change the parent or the position among the siblings <code>remove</code> remove a node; a removed surface becomes detached <code>configure</code> send size, toplevel states (activated, tiled, maximized, fullscreen) and decoration mode to a client <code>focus</code> set the keyboard focus to an own surface, or clear it without a surface; a client that cleared the focus may give it back once to the surface that had it, also of another client <code>close</code> ask a client to close a surface <code>camera</code> set the camera of an output, or restore its default camera without a transform; with a <code>duration</code>, move it there; the first client that sets the camera owns it, and a <code>camera</code> without a transform gives it up <p><code>animate</code> lets plugins and agents animate without code in every frame:</p> <pre><code>{"animate": {"id": "frame", "props": {"opacity": 0, "visible": false},
             "duration": 300, "easing": "ease_out"}}
</code></pre> <p>The core moves <code>transform</code>, <code>opacity</code>, <code>size</code> and <code>color</code> toward the targets along the curve: <code>linear</code> (the default), <code>ease_in</code>, <code>ease_out</code> or <code>ease_in_out</code>. The other properties change at the end, so this example fades the node out and then hides it. The duration is in milliseconds, at most one minute. A later <code>animate</code> or <code>update</code> of the node ends the animation where it is. The end sends <code>animation.done</code>.</p> <p>A camera moves the same way, with <code>duration</code> and <code>easing</code>. It starts where the camera is now, also in the middle of another move, and the end sends <code>animation.done</code> with the output and then <code>output.changed</code>:</p> <pre><code>{"camera": {"output": "DP-1", "transform": {"scale": 2, "translate": [-640, -400]},
            "duration": 500, "easing": "ease_in_out"}}
</code></pre>
